   1   
      Title Optimization model for Glen Canyon Dam releases to favor Bugs popula
      tion (June 2018)
       
       
      ###################################
      Created By: Moazzam Ali Rind
      Email: moazzamalirind@gmail.com
       
      Created : 4/3/2021
       
       
      Description: This model is designed to validate the Weekend-Weekday model 
      at the hourly time scale. Since this a validation model, therefore, the hy
      drograph is input to the model.
                   Which also means there is no release decision involved in thi
      s model. The aim of validation model is to simulate the observed hydrograp
      h and estimate the hydropower revenue from the model.
       
      ######################################
       
  19   
  20  **** Hourly validation Model code:
  21   
  22  Set
  23   
  24            d             days in June
  25            p             time periods during a day /p1*p24/
  26            modpar        Saving model parameter for each of the scenario/ M
      odStat "Model Status", SolStat "Solve Status"/
  27   
  28   
  29  *======================================
  30  *Parameters
  31  *======================================
  32   
  33  PARAMETERS
  34   
  35  initstorage                  Initial reservoir storage on 1st June 2018 (a
      cre-ft)/12948951/
  36  maxstorage                   Reservoir capacity (acre-ft)/25000000/
  37  minstorage                   Minimum reservoir storage to maintain hydropo
      wer level(acre-ft) /8950000/
  38  Inflow(d)                    Inflow to reservoir (cfs)
  39  observed_release(d,p)        observed release during June 2018 averaged ov
      er hourly timestep (cfs)
  40  maxRel                       Maximum release in a day d at any timeperiod 
      p(cfs)/31500/
  41  minRel                       Minimum release in a day d at any timeperiod 
      p(cfs)/8000/
  42  evap(d)                      Evaporation (ac-ft per day).
  43  EnergyRate(p)                Energy revenue ($ per MWH)
  44   
  45  FStore                       Storing objective function value
  46  Xstore(d)                    Storing energy generation(MWh per day)
  47  ModelResults(modpar)         Store solution status of the scenarios i.e. w
      hether the solution found is optimal or not?
  48  RStore(d,p)                  Store Release values during each period (cfs)
  49  Sstore(d)                    Store Storage Values (ac-ft)
  50  ;
  51   
  52   
  53   
  54  *===================================================
  55  * Read data from Excel
  56  *===================================================
  58   
  59  *Write the input Data into a GDX file
GDXIN   E:\OneDrive - Washington State University (email.wsu.edu)\Documents\GitH
        ub\BugFlowExperiment_Analysis2026\Validation\June\Weekend-Weekday&Hourly
        \Valid_June2018(Hourly).gdx
  61   
  62  * parameters and input data from the GDX file into the model
--- LOAD  d = 3:d
--- LOAD  Inflow = 4:Inflow
--- LOAD  observed_release = 1:observed_release
--- LOAD  EnergyRate = 2:EnergyRate
--- LOAD  evap = 5:evap
  68  *Close the GDX file
  70   
  71  Display d,inflow, p, EnergyRate,observed_release,evap;
  72  *===============================================
  73  SCALAR
  74  Convert                       conversion factor from cfs to ac-ft per hour
       (0.0014*60)/0.083/
  75  Daily_RelRange                Allowable daily release change range (cfs)/8
      000/
  76   
  77  VARIABLES
  78  ObjectiveVal                   Objective function value
  79   
  80  Positive Variables
  81  storage(d)                    reservoir storage on any day d (acre-ft)
  82  release(d,p)                  reservoir release on any day d in any period
       p (cfs)
  83  Energy_Gen(d,p)               Hydropower Generated at a each time step (MW
      H)
  84  ReleaseVol(d,p)               volume of water released per time step(acre-
      ft)
  85  Vol_monthlyrelease            Total volume of water released in the month
  86  ;
  87   
  88   
  89   
  90  EQUATIONS
  91  *AND CONSTRAINTS
  92   
  93  EQ1__ResMassBal(d)           Reservoir mass balance (acre-ft)
  94  EQ2__reqpowerstorage(d)      The minimum storage equivalent to reservoir l
      evel required for hydropower generation (acre-ft)
  95  EQ3__maxstor(d)              Reservoir storage max (acre-ft)
  96  EQ4__MaxR(d,p)               Max Release (cfs)
  97  EQ5__MinR(d,p)               Min Release (cfs)
  98  EQ6_Rel_Range(d,p)           Constraining the daily release range on a wee
      kday (cfs per day)
  99  EQ7_FlowVolume(d,p)          volume of water released per time step (acre-
      ft)
 100  EQ8__March_rel               Total monthly volume of water released(acre-f
      t)
 101  EQ9_EnergyGen(d,p)           Amount of energy generated in each time step 
      (MWH)
 102  EQ10_EnergyGen_Max(d,p)      Maximum Energy Generation Limit of the Glen C
      aynon Dam(MWh)
 103  EQ11_EnergyRevenue           Total monthly Hydropower Revenue generated
 104  EQ12_ReleaseSim(d,p)         Setting release values as predefined for simu
      lation(cfs)
 105  ;
 106   
 107   
 108  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
 109   
 110  EQ1__ResMassBal(d)..         storage(d) =e= initstorage$(ord(d)eq 1)+ stor
      age(d-1)$(ord(d)gt 1)+ (inflow(d)*Convert*24)- sum(p,ReleaseVol(d,p))-evap
      (d);
 111  EQ2__reqpowerstorage(d)..    storage(d) =g= minstorage;
 112  EQ3__maxstor(d)..            storage(d)=l= maxstorage;
 113  EQ4__MaxR(d,p)..             release(d,p)=l= maxRel ;
 114  EQ5__MinR(d,p)..             release(d,p)=g= minRel;
 115  EQ6_Rel_Range(d,p)..         release(d,p+1)-release(d,p)=l=Daily_RelRange;
 116  EQ7_FlowVolume(d,p)..        ReleaseVol(d,p) =e= release(d,p)*Convert;
 117  EQ8__March_rel..             sum(d,sum(p,ReleaseVol(d,p)))=e=Vol_monthlyre
      lease;
 118  EQ9_EnergyGen(d,p)..         Energy_Gen(d,p)=e= release(d,p)*0.03715;
 119  EQ10_EnergyGen_Max(d,p)..    Energy_Gen(d,p)=l= 1320;
 120  *Maximum Energy Generation capacity of GCD (MWH).. Source https://www.usbr
      .gov/uc/rm/crsp/gc/
 121   
 122  **EQ11_HyrdroPower objective
 123  EQ11_EnergyRevenue..                           ObjectiveVal=e= sum((d,p),E
      nergy_Gen(d,p)*EnergyRate(p));
 124   
 125   
 126  ***************************************************
 127  ******Simulation Model
 128  ****************************************** ********
 129  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
 130  *Eqauation 12 is making releases equal to observed release.
 131  EQ12_ReleaseSim(d,p)..                 release(d,p)=e=observed_release(d,p
      );
 132   
 133   
 134  * Define MODEL validation using the LP
 135  MODEL validation Find extreme points by using  LP /ALL/;
 136  *Solve the model
 137  SOLVE validation USING LP MAXIMIGING ObjectiveVal;
 138  FStore = ObjectiveVal.L;
 139  ModelResults("ModStat")= validation.modelstat;
 140  ModelResults("SolStat")= validation.solvestat;
 141  RStore(d,p)= release.L(d,p);
 142  Sstore(d)= storage.L(d);
 143  Xstore(d)= sum(p,Energy_Gen.L(d,p));
 144   
 145  DISPLAY FStore,RStore,Sstore,Xstore;
 146   
 147  * Dump all input data and results to a GAMS gdx file
 148  Execute_Unload "Valid_June2018(Hourly).gdx";
 149  * Dump the gdx file to an Excel workbook
 150  Execute "gdx2xls Valid_June2018(Hourly).gdx"
 151   
 152   
 153   
